From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:49:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Close the connections of windows whose event loop
 died

The IndexedDB manager forgets a global's connections when the global's
teardown sends AbortPendingUpgrades, which Window::clear_js_runtime and
the end of a worker's event loop do. A window whose script thread
panics, or whose content process dies, never sends it; its connections
stayed open in the backend, and since deletes and upgrades wait for open
connections, every later delete and upgrade of their databases waited
until the browser restarted.

Open requests now carry the pipeline of their window (None for workers,
which close their connections when their event loop ends, also when it
ends with a panic). When the constellation handles a panic of an event
loop, or a failed send to a pipeline, which means its event loop is
gone, it sends both storage groups
SyncOperation::CloseConnectionsOfPipelines with the event loop's
pipelines. The manager rolls back and finishes the transactions of those
windows' connections, closes the connections, and ends their open
requests as AbortPendingUpgrades does, reverting a running upgrade.

Validation: host `cargo nextest run -p servo-storage -p servo-storage-traits` at this commit: 164 passed, 1 skipped (new test_indexeddb_connections_of_a_crashed_window_close: a delete that waits for a crashed window's connection, which has a live readwrite transaction, finishes with the old version once the pipeline is reported, and the window's running first upgrade is reverted, so the next open upgrades from 0); host SM release builds at this commit; `./mach check --ohos` of servo-storage with SQLite, RDB and both: no warnings; WPT and the board on the stack tip as in the previous commit. Not run: a real script-thread panic or content-process crash, as nothing in the test suites causes one
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent implemented the pipeline tagging, the manager's close and the constellation hook, and wrote the integration test)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
